  62	/// This is deliberately smaller than the general LZ4 compression bound. The
  63	/// compressed representation includes an additional slice compared to a
  64	/// resident terminal page, so an encoded block which fills more than this
  65	/// buffer cannot reduce resident memory. Limiting the output here lets a
  66	/// PageList borrow a standard page-pool item as scratch instead of retaining a
  67	/// larger, compression-bound allocation.
  68	///
